  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-Sectoral Assistance to Displaced Populations in the Lac Province, Chad</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Lac Province of Chad has experienced a protracted internal displacement situation since the start of the Boko Haram crisis in 2014, with over 240,000 persons currently displaced internally across 281 displacement sites. While armed non-state actors remain active in the region, the general security situation has improved, creating pockets of stability which are conducive to durable solutions. However, seasonal instability due to flooding and localized violence foment micro-displacements towards the east of the province away from the shoreline of the Lake, exacerbating vulnerabilities. The resulting situation is a mixture of protracted and new displacements in a volatile and remote region with persistent development challenges. Within this context, limited access to services and infrastructure continue to engender precarity and signify that displaced populations remain dependent on humanitarian assistance to meet their basic needs. Through adopting a multi-sectoral, gender-sensitive approach &#x2013; focusing on shelter and water, sanitation and hygiene while collecting robust data on displacement trends to help tailor the intervention &#x2013; this project contributes towards bolstering communities&#x2019; resilience and decreasing the likelihood of subsequent displacement.</narrative>
  </description>
